course: dictionary
lesson: 1681
title: Chosen and picked
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chosen means picked out from a group as the one you want. «You have been chosen to be class captain» means that someone looked at the whole class and picked you.
explain: Chosen is the past form of choose, so you will often see it after have, has or was: «I have chosen a book», «The team was chosen on Monday». It can also describe a thing that has been picked, like the chosen team.
explain: Check the words around it. «Carefully chosen» means picked with thought and care. Ask yourself: was something picked out from a group? If it was, chosen fits.
fact: Chosen means picked from a group as the one you want.
fact: «Chosen» is the past form of choose, used with have, has and was: «I have chosen a book».
fact: As an adjective, «chosen» describes something that has been selected: «the chosen team».
fact: «Chosen one» means a hero picked by fate to do something special, as in many stories.
fact: «Carefully chosen» means picked with thought and care.
exercise: «You have been chosen to be class captain.» What does chosen mean here? | Thrown away and forgotten | *Picked from the group as the one wanted | Painted in bright colours | Lost in the crowd
exercise: Most consoles have parental controls that can block games above a «chosen age rating». What is chosen? | *The age rating that was picked for blocking | The console that is broken | The game that is always free | The room where the console sits
exercise: Which word in this sentence is the past form of choose? «I have chosen a book from the shelf.» | from | book | shelf | *chosen
test: «Parental controls can ask for a PIN before films above a chosen age will play.» What does chosen age mean? | *An age that was picked as the limit | The youngest age of all | A random age nobody has thought about | The age of the film's main actor
test: Which phrase means picked with thought and care? | Lost on the bus | Broken in two | Hastily thrown | *Carefully chosen
exam: In «the chosen one saved the village», what is chosen doing? | Showing the village is burning | *Describing the hero as someone picked by fate for a special job | Asking a question | Telling us the hero is a dog
